    <system:String x:Key="Guide_GettingStarted_Body">Ongenet opens on a demo song so you can press Space to hear the engine immediately.&#10;&#10;• File → New / Open / Save — standard project workflow (.ongen format).&#10;• The Library sidebar (right) holds demo projects, instruments, effects, and samples.&#10;• Settings (title bar) — pick audio/MIDI devices, theme, control surface, and shortcuts.&#10;• Autosave backups land in your app data folder; recovery is offered on launch when a newer backup exists.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Samples_Body">Good sources for one-shots, loops, and instruments you can use legally in your projects. Always check each pack's licence — CC0 needs no attribution; Creative Commons may require credit in your album notes.&#10;&#10;• Download packs, then add the folder in Settings → Library → Sample folders.&#10;• Drag files from Library → Samples onto an audio track.&#10;• Enable Auto-stretch (Library options) to sync loops to your project tempo on import.&#10;• SFZ instruments and soundfonts go in Library → Soundfonts once their folders are added.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Plugins_Body">Ongenet hosts CLAP, LV2, VST2/VST3, and Audio Units (macOS). Plugins are scanned in the background at launch and appear in Library → Instruments / FX and in track effect menus.&#10;&#10;• Install into the standard OS plugin folders or set CLAP_PATH, VST_PATH, VST3_PATH, LV2_PATH.&#10;• Rescans pick up new files on the next launch — no manual refresh needed.&#10;&#10;Suggested starters (all free or FOSS):&#10;• Synths — Surge XT, Odin 2, Helm, Vital (free), TAL-NoiseMaker, u-he Tyrell N6.&#10;• Effects — ChowDSP suite, Dragonfly Reverb, LSP Plugins (LV2), Melda free bundle, TAL-Reverb-4.&#10;• Samplers — Decent Sampler, PianoBook SFZ packs.&#10;&#10;Install paths:&#10;• macOS CLAP/VST3/AU: ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/…&#10;• Linux LV2: ~/.lv2 or /usr/lib/lv2&#10;• Windows VST3: %CommonProgramFiles%\VST3</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Sidechain_Body">Sidechaining ducks one sound when another is loud — the pumping heard in EDM when the kick hits.&#10;&#10;Built-in Sidechain effect (track FX chain):&#10;• No source selected — tempo-synced pump (classic ghost-kick); set Rate and Amount.&#10;• Pick a source track (e.g. kick) — ducks whenever that track is loud; tweak Attack and Release.&#10;&#10;Compressor with sidechain:&#10;• Add Compressor to the bass/pad chain; pick the kick as Sidechain source for envelope-style ducking.&#10;&#10;Track order matters — the sidechain source track is processed before tracks that read from it.&#10;&#10;Alternative: Volume LFO on the track inspector gives rhythmic pump/tremolo without an envelope follower.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Production_Body">Practical habits that keep mixes clean and sessions fast.&#10;&#10;• Gain staging — keep faders near unity; trim hot recordings or clips before heavy plugin chains.&#10;• Aux sends — route to reverb/delay returns instead of inserting the same effect on every track.&#10;• Freeze / render — right-click clips or freeze CPU-heavy instrument tracks.&#10;• Groove — apply swing templates in Groove settings for humanized timing.&#10;• MIDI FX — arp, chord, and scale processors on instrument tracks before the synth.&#10;• Comping — loop-record take lanes, pick regions, flatten the best performance.&#10;• Reference mix — export stems and A/B against commercial tracks at matched loudness.&#10;• Surround — use surround pan in the mixer when bouncing 5.1/7.1 for film and immersive work.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Timeline_Body">The arrange view is the center of the window.&#10;&#10;• Add tracks from the track header menu; arm for recording, mute/solo from the header or mixer.&#10;• Drag audio from the Library onto a track; enable Auto-stretch in Settings if you want tempo sync on import.&#10;• MIDI clips open in the piano roll (bottom panel). Audio clips show warp markers and fades on the timeline.&#10;• Right-click clips for render, freeze, linked copies, stem separation, and audio-to-MIDI conversion.&#10;• Comping: loop-record into take lanes, then pick the best regions and flatten.&#10;• Ripple edit: Ctrl+Shift+I inserts a bar at the playhead; Ctrl+Shift+Backspace deletes a bar and closes the gap.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Session_Body">Hybrid workflows combine timeline arrangement with launcher-style playback.&#10;&#10;• Session tab — clip slots per track/scene; launch clips while the transport runs.&#10;• Channel Rack + Pattern editor — FL-style step grids; change pattern length and step count in the pattern toolbar.&#10;• Pattern clips on the timeline expand into MIDI at playback via the pattern scheduler.&#10;• Section Playlist (View menu) — play arrangement markers in order for song-structure previews.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Field_Body">Field is Ongenet's node-graph instrument and effect (similar in spirit to Bitwig Grid).&#10;&#10;• Add a Field instrument or effect from the built-in list or open the Field editor from an instrument slot.&#10;• Patch oscillators, envelopes, filters, and math nodes; use Scale Quantize / Key Root for theory-aware patches.&#10;• Factory Field patches ship in the instrument/FX preset library — editable graphs, not black boxes.&#10;• Module nodes wrap any built-in or hosted plugin as a patchable block inside Field.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Mixer_Body">• Mixer tab — per-track volume, pan, sends, input monitor, surround pan, and routing matrix.&#10;• Export (title bar) — master mix, stems, regions, surround offline; timeline XML for post handoff (not binary AAF).&#10;• Transport bar Export button mirrors the dialog; MIDI export is available from the transport area.&#10;• Collaboration folder sync (Export menu) copies the project + manifest for folder-based sharing.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Shortcuts_Body">Global (when not typing in a text field):&#10;&#10;Ctrl+N  New          Ctrl+O  Open         Ctrl+S  Save&#10;Ctrl+Shift+S  Save As    Ctrl+Z  Undo    Ctrl+Y / Ctrl+Shift+Z  Redo&#10;Space   Play/stop    Ctrl+Alt+T  Tempo map    Ctrl+Alt+L  Section playlist&#10;Ctrl+Shift+I  Ripple insert bar    Ctrl+Shift+Backspace  Ripple delete bar&#10;Shift+[ / Shift+]  Set loop in/out to start marker    F8  Renderer diagnostics&#10;&#10;Timeline (focus timeline first): Delete — remove clip; Ctrl+D — duplicate.&#10;Piano roll (focus piano roll): Delete — remove selected notes.&#10;&#10;Typing keyboard: Z-row and Q-row play notes on instrument tracks (FL-style map).&#10;Customize ripple/tempo/playlist shortcuts in Settings → MIDI → Keyboard shortcuts.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AudioEditor_Title">Audio Editor</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AudioEditor_Body">The standalone Audio Editor (View → Audio Editor) is Edison-class sample surgery.&#10;&#10;• Open clips from the timeline via right-click → Open in Audio Editor; stack multiple clips as lanes.&#10;• Cut, copy, paste, trim, spectral overlay, normalize, fades — same engine as the Sample Inspector.&#10;• Double-click the waveform to audition from that point; middle-drag to zoom.&#10;• Edits to shared buffers affect every clip referencing the same source.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_PitchEditor_Title">Polyphonic pitch</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_PitchEditor_Body">Built-in VariAudio-class pitch correction — no Melodyne licence required.&#10;&#10;• Right-click an audio clip → Open Pitch Editor.&#10;• Analyze to seed note segments from polyphonic detection; drag pitch cents per blob.&#10;• Changes play back in real time with crossfades; flatten via Render clip to new track if needed.&#10;• Manual editing is the reliability backstop when detection misses notes.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Scripting_Title">Scripting</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Scripting_Body">Centre **Scripting** tab runs C# automation against the open project.&#10;&#10;• Factory scripts under the app folder and your Documents/Ongenet/Scripts folder — use them as examples.&#10;• Edit scripts in the built-in IDE (syntax highlighting, diagnostics, IntelliSense).&#10;• **Export project** / **Export preset** generate portable C# you can rerun anywhere (no audio blobs — re-link samples).&#10;• Batch Run executes top-level statements once; Start live keeps handler subscriptions active.&#10;• Scripts receive a global api object (IScriptingApi) for project, transport, tracks, devices, clips, automation, and patterns.&#10;• api.Log() writes to the output panel; Pop out opens a separate window sharing the same session.&#10;• All mutating calls capture undo automatically. Desktop only — only run scripts you trust.</system:String>
